If it's blessed it reduces items weights to 1/4. If it's not (and not=20
cursed of course) it reduces weight to 1/2. And you should never open=20
cursed bags of holding unless you have to as you might loose items in=20
the bag at random. One good thing to know is that bags of holding are=20
never cursed when you find them, they have to get cursed by some=20
(usually monster) action.

It's easy to test. Pick up things one at a time until one item makes=20
you burdened. Then put something one or more things into the bag and=20
you'll notice you become unburdened again.

If you aren't used to bags of holding don't try to be overly clever=20
using them. You can't put a bag of holding inside another and hope for=20
1/16. In fact there are some other items you shouldn't put into a (such=20
a magical) bag of holding either.=20

(and before someone tries to correct me :->, you can put bags of=20
holding into other bags of holding in a very convoluted way you=20
shouldn't bother yourself with at this point)

